            "endSeconds": 3925,
            "summary": "As Clifford PTO president, she expressed concern about the impact of multi-grade split classes on students and teachers, and urged that IEP administrative support be maintained, arguing that true equity means ensuring each school has what it needs."
          },
          {
            "name": "Steve Yake",
            "startSeconds": 3936,
            "endSeconds": 4113,
            "summary": "As Orion School Site Council chair, he expressed concern that cutting the guest teacher would directly impact the classroom, especially given Orion's Mandarin program needs, and asked whether all district-level cuts had truly been exhausted before reaching school sites."
          },
          {
            "name": "Tina Mercer",
            "startSeconds": 4119,
            "endSeconds": 4257,
            "summary": "As Roosevelt Elementary principal and committee member, she thanked Dr. Baker for keeping the heaviest cuts at the district level and expressed appreciation for retaining halftime guest teachers and Pre-K through 5 IEP administrative support."
